 But we standardized Wi-Fi for several years

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.920 align:start position:0%
 and it sort of went nowhere.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.760 align:start position:0%
 There's a few access points and so on.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.040 align:start position:0%
 And then we put it into a volume platform

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.960 align:start position:0%
 that we drove into the industry and all of a sudden,

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.800 align:start position:0%
 every coffee shop, every hotel, every office,

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.320 align:start position:0%
 became wirelessly enabled.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.840 align:start position:0%
 It changed the platform.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.320 align:start position:0%
 It changed the use cases.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:06.160 align:start position:0%
 And this is exactly what we're doing with the AI PC.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:13.040 align:start position:0%
 We're Intel is driving this new platform evolution, the AI PC.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.440 align:start position:0%
 We're ramping core ultra rapidly.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:16.960 align:start position:0%
 And when we launched it in December,

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.480 align:start position:0%
 we had great response from the industry.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.440 align:start position:0%
 Today, we've already shipped over 5 million units.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.480 align:start position:0%
 We're on track, you know, right, MJ?

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.560 align:start position:0%
 On track, you know, to meet or beat our 40 million unit

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:30.880 align:start position:0%
 goal this year, 100 plus million next year.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.440 align:start position:0%
 You know, we are underway.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:36.720 align:start position:0%
 We just launched the commercial versions in February of core

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.560 align:start position:0%
 ultra.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:41.560 align:start position:0%
 You know, we're expanding our AI PC developer program.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:46.480 align:start position:0%
 Also, and now, IHVs and ISV programs to go with it.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.160 align:start position:0%
 500 plus AI models are now optimized for core ultra.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.480 align:start position:0%
 And of course, working with our OEM partners,

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.560 align:start position:0%
 Dell, HP, Lenovo, our roadmap is strong,

00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:00.000 align:start position:0%
 off to a good start, but with lunar lake,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.360 align:start position:0%
 air lake, Panther Lake, the roadmap is strong.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.400 align:start position:0%
 And in particular, I'm quite excited about the next platform,

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:09.880 align:start position:0%
 you know, where before competitors ship their first chips,

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.320 align:start position:0%
 you know, we're launching our second, you know,

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.160 align:start position:0%
 lunar lake 3XDI performance.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:26.600 align:start position:0%
 This little marble has over 100 platform tops, 45 NPU tops

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.280 align:start position:0%
 alone.

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.240 align:start position:0%
 And before others get started, we're

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:32.560 align:start position:0%
 on to the second generation, the third generation's in fab,

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:36.760 align:start position:0%
 because we're going to drive the AI PC category to every

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.760 align:start position:0%
 fingertip of your users and your customers.

