00:55:12.360 --> 00:55:14.960 align:start position:0%
 So when we have an incident on a fab equipment,

00:55:14.960 --> 00:55:17.480 align:start position:0%
 we want to find out if similar incidents have occurred

00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:20.280 align:start position:0%
 in the past so that we can understand the root cause

00:55:20.280 --> 00:55:21.520 align:start position:0%
 and resolve them.

00:55:21.520 --> 00:55:25.560 align:start position:0%
 And this is so that we can get the equipment back up quickly.

00:55:25.560 --> 00:55:28.600 align:start position:0%
 Fortunately, we have a huge amount of structured

00:55:28.600 --> 00:55:31.240 align:start position:0%
 and unstructured data spanning decades

00:55:31.240 --> 00:55:34.840 align:start position:0%
 and millions of records documenting our operations.

00:55:34.840 --> 00:55:37.240 align:start position:0%
 We can reference this massive body of data

00:55:37.240 --> 00:55:40.400 align:start position:0%
 to find a resolution to get the equipment back up.

00:55:40.400 --> 00:55:44.240 align:start position:0%
 However, this process is time consuming and can take hours

00:55:44.240 --> 00:55:46.120 align:start position:0%
 and sometimes even days.

00:55:46.120 --> 00:55:48.000 align:start position:0%
